(i) Reflecting dominant influence to appoint or remove directors/ senior
management;

(ii) Having the power of attorney over the entity;

(iii)Owning stocks or rights over outstanding debts that are convertible into
voting equity;

(iv)Participating in the financing of the enterprise; or

(v)Having control through trusts, agreements, arrangements, understandings,
policies or practices, close and intimate family relationships or if a company
defaults on certain payments.
